---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Portfolio Lab"
  description="Privacy policy for Portfolio Lab. All computation is client-side; no data is collected."
>
  <div class="spine page-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short version: nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose-spine prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Portfolio Lab is a <strong>100% static, client-side site</strong>. All computation
      runs in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. No account. No email. No analytics (unless Cloudflare Analytics is enabled,
      in which case only anonymous page-view counts — no personal data, no cookies).
    </p>

    <h2>Local storage</h2>
    <p>
      Your questionnaire answers and portfolio preferences are saved to
      <code>localStorage</code> in your browser so you can return to your session.
      This data never leaves your device. Clear your browser storage to remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>External resources</h2>
    <p>
      Google Fonts is loaded for typography (Inter Tight, Fraunces, JetBrains Mono).
      This is the only external call made by the page. No other third-party scripts
      are loaded.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href="https://oriz.in/contact/">oriz.in/contact</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
